~ A live HTTP GET with the `core.http` client: `get` builds the request, sends it over
~ core.net's `@tcpRequest`, and parses the reply into `Ok(Response)`. We assert the
~ request succeeded, the status is 200, and the body is the expected page. `<< core.test`
~ verifies each result; on success the program exits 0.
~ NOTE: this makes a LIVE network call to example.com:80 when run.
<< core.http
<< core.test

^ = () -> $ => <
  result :: Result = get("http://example.com/")
  assertOk(result)
  response :: Response = result ?
    | Ok(page)  => page
    | NotOk(_)  => Response { raw = "" }
  assertEq(status(response), 200)
  assert(body(response).contains("Example Domain"))
>
